  "step_3": "The information relevant to the decision reason (skewness) is that Lottery A has a higher probability of the unfavorable outcome (0 Euros, 80% vs. 75%), which makes it more right-skewed. However, the individual does not mention this aspect at all. Instead, the individual compares the chance of winning and the prize size, suggesting a preference for the higher prize despite a slightly lower probability. There is no reference to the probability of zero payoff or to skewness. Therefore, the individual did not consider the skewness of the lotteries or apply the rule that prefers the more right-skewed lottery. The justification is based on different grounds (prize size and probability of winning), not on skewness. Hence, the decision reason was not used.",
  "final_assessment_score": 0
